From 2a53d7c2d65626f3f8201907433a86c9834e12b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] arm64: topology: no warning without an architected timer
 frequency

freq_inv_set_max_ratio() takes the architected timer's frequency as the
reference of the activity monitors' frequency invariance, and warns when
it reads 0. On the SM-T715 (Exynos5433) started at EL2 by its own loader
the generic counter does not run and CNTFRQ reads 0; the kernel keeps
time on the MCT. The first cpufreq policy then printed
"WARNING: CPU: 2 PID: 55 at arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c:125" (test
cpuf1, 2026-11-24). These Cortex-A53 and A57 have no AMU, so nothing is
lost: return quietly when the reference is 0, and keep the warning for a
maximum frequency of 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c
index 052e9b994..6cc986840 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/topology.c
@@ -121,7 +121,19 @@ void freq_inv_set_max_ratio(int cpu, u64 max_rate)
 {
 	u64 ratio, ref_rate = arch_timer_get_rate();
 
-	if (unlikely(!max_rate || !ref_rate)) {
+	/*
+	 * No architected timer frequency (CNTFRQ reads 0, as on an Exynos5433
+	 * started at EL2 by the SM-T715's own loader, where the kernel keeps
+	 * time on the MCT): there is no reference for the activity monitors'
+	 * invariance, and these cores have no AMU to need one.  cpufreq's own
+	 * frequency invariance still applies.
+	 */
+	if (!ref_rate) {
+		pr_debug("CPU%d: no architected timer frequency: no AMU frequency invariance\n", cpu);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (unlikely(!max_rate)) {
 		WARN_ONCE(1, "CPU%d: invalid maximum or reference frequency.\n",
 			 cpu);
 		return;
-- 
